# Import Sorting — Shortest To Longest

When adding, editing, or reviewing imports in any JS/TS file, order every
top-level `import` statement by the **full character length of the line**, from
**shortest to longest**.

## Rules

- Compare the entire import line length (including `import`, quotes, and `;`).
- Shorter lines come first; longer lines last.
- On equal length, keep the original relative order (stable sort).
- Only reorder the contiguous block(s) of top-level imports. Do not move imports
  past side-effectful ones (e.g. `import './setup'`) if that changes behavior.
- Do not change import contents, just their order.

## Example

```typescript
// ❌ BAD (unordered)
import { configService } from '../services/configService';
import fs from 'fs';
import express, { Express } from 'express';
import cors from 'cors';

// ✅ GOOD (shortest → longest)
import fs from 'fs';
import cors from 'cors';
import express, { Express } from 'express';
import { configService } from '../services/configService';
```
